":"success","api_error_status":null,"result":"I approve PKT-0011. The only file changed is the new test file `tests/unit/formatchecker.tests.js` (576 lines), so it stays within the 2-file and 800-line budget, and production code is untouched.\n\n**Against the goal**\n- **Extension mapping:** every known extension is tested both ways (extension to format id and back). Aliases, `pdfa`→`pdf`, upper-case, unknown, empty, null, a leading dot or space, non-string input and the one-way ids are covered too. A sanity test checks the table's format ids are all defined and distinct, which guards against a wrong constant name passing silently.\n- **Classification:** one table runs every format id through all five predicates and checks each answer exactly (`toBe(true)` / `toBe(false)`). It includes the canvas, TeamLab, PDF-family and unknown ids.\n- **Signature detection:** all buffers are built in memory, with no binary fixture files. Each image type has a positive case, plus empty, truncated, null (checks the error is logged) and the 1000-byte SVG search limit. The tests also pin that only xlsx is detected inside a ZIP, that the marker is searched only in the last 8KB (both sides of the limit), which ZIP header variants are accepted, and that null input throws.\n- **`getAllFormats`:** checks the category keys and how a small JSON file is sorted into them, without snapshotting the whole list. It also covers skipping malformed entries, caching per file path, retrying after an unreadable file, invalid JSON, non-array JSON and the call without a context.\n\n**What the automated checks would not catch:** the assertions are characterizations, not fixes. Odd behaviors (the null `TypeError`, no `%PDF` detection, the rejection when no context is passed) are pinned as they are today. Temporary directories are cleaned up in `afterAll`.\n\n**Remaining gap:** the previous review asked for the surprising behaviors to be written in the packet's Executor log. That log still doesn't list them.